{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "דברו אל בני ישראל", :translit "dabru el b'nei yisra'el", :gloss "Speak to the children of Israel"} {:he "ובפ' נגעים לא אמר דברו", :translit "uv'parashat nega'im lo amar dabru", :gloss "and in the parashah of nega'im it does not say 'speak'"} {:he "באו נגעים על ישראל", :translit "ba'u nega'im al yisra'el", :gloss "nega'im came upon Israel"} {:he "וסמך פרשת זב למצורע", :translit "vesamach parashat zav lametzora", :gloss "and the parashah of the zav is juxtaposed to the metzora"} {:he "והנחש בצרעת", :translit "vehanachash b'tzara'at", :gloss "and the serpent with tzara'at"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition of parashat zav next to parashat metzora explained via serpent narrative: serpent punished with tzara'at, woman cursed with zivah."}], :frame {:text "The Talmud states that through the golden calf which Aaron made, nega'im came upon Israel (Avodah Zarah 44b). A baraitha cited in tractate Shabbat 56a teaches that the serpent infected Eve with zivah. The serpent itself was afflicted with tzara'at as part of its curse (Genesis 3:14, as elaborated in Bereshit Rabbah 20:5). The juxtaposition of the zav and metzora sections traces both afflictions back to the serpent's act.", :sources ["Avodah Zarah 44b" "Shabbat 56a" "Genesis 3:14" "Bereshit Rabbah 20:5"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition of parashat zav next to parashat metzora explained via serpent narrative: serpent punished with tzara'at, woman cursed with zivah.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:23:28.905654658Z", :model "glm-5.2"}